      "designator": "CS23-0",
      "grouping_at_time": "Subpart B \u2014 Flight",
      "title_at_revision": "Longitudinal stability and control",
      "text": "(a) A landplane may have no uncontrollable tendency to nose over in any reasonably expected operating condition, including rebound during landing or take-off. Wheel brakes must operate smoothly and may not induce any undue tendency to nose over.\n(b) A seaplane or amphibian may not have dangerous or uncontrollable purpoising characteristics at any normal operating speed on the water.",
